WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.800
Hey there, welcome to Models and Agents for Beginners.

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:07.220
Episode 111 is July 23rd, 2026.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.000
Some awesome AI developments today,

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.100
and we're going to make all of it make sense.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:13.480
Let's get into it.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.120
Here's something that's going to change how you capture

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:17.900
and remix your everyday moments.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.580
A new wearable device called Ikyros

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:23.880
quietly records short clips of family life around you.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.300
It then uses AI to turn those real moments

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.340
into artistic pictures or videos

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.960
that still feel personal.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:33.020
Think of it like a sketch artist

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:34.900
who trails behind you all day,

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.000
capturing scenes and instantly redrawing them

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:38.940
in new styles.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:40.880
Another way to picture this

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.920
is like a memory remix machine

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:44.480
that takes your actual day

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.480
and spins it into something creative

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.480
without any extra work from you.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:51.020
The device draws from the spirit

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:53.600
of an older friendly robot called Gibo,

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.680
but makes the idea portable

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.220
so you can clip it on or set it nearby.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:00.760
This matters because creative tools

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.360
are shifting from phone screens

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:04.800
into things you wear or keep on a shelf.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.640
For someone who enjoys making TikToks

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:09.060
or editing photos for fun,

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:12.140
it opens a new path to turn ordinary days

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:13.320
into shareable art.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.760
You do not need to learn complicated editing software

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.220
since the AI handles the remixing step.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.760
Privacy questions come up too

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:24.060
since a gadget that watches all the time

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.940
needs clear rules about what it records and shares.

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:29.440
If tools like this become common,

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:31.740
your future creative projects could start

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.640
with real life instead of typing prompts from scratch.

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:38.580
You might one day point a small device at a birthday party

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:40.500
and get back a stylized video

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.160
that looks like a movie scene.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.620
Right now, the product is still new

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:47.000
so the best way to explore similar ideas

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.300
is to try free AI image and video tools

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.460
that already exist.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:54.560
Okay, now for my favorite part of the show

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:57.900
where we slow down and see how one piece of this technology

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.560
actually works under the hood.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.800
You know how when you take a bunch of photos on your phone,

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:05.440
your brain can look at them and instantly remember

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:07.320
the story of what happened that day.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.340
Now picture an AI that does something similar but backwards.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:13.740
It looks at short clips or photos

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:15.520
you just recorded then guesses

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:18.320
what a new version of those moments could look like

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.480
if they were drawn in a different style.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:23.520
Imagine the AI treating each scene

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.360
like a puzzle made of shapes, colors, and movement.

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:29.400
It breaks the puzzle apart then rebuilds it

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:32.360
using patterns it learned from millions of other pictures

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:32.980
and videos.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.520
Each new frame it creates is basically the AI

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:38.580
asking what this scene would look like

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:40.640
if it were painted like an old cartoon

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.420
or filmed like a music video.

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:45.500
The more examples the AI has seen before,

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.760
the better it gets at making the new version

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.680
feel natural instead of random.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:52.720
That is why some AI videos look smooth

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:54.040
and others look weird.

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:57.440
Think of the process like auto-complete on your phone

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.240
but for images and motion instead of words.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:04.320
The AI never actually understands the moment the way you do.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:07.820
It is only rearranging patterns it has seen before.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:10.540
The same way auto-complete rearranges words

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:12.280
it has seen in other texts.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:16.500
That simple rearrangement idea is what lets the system create

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.360
fresh art from your real clips

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:21.120
without needing to invent brand new rules from nothing.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:24.600
And that is how these tools turn everyday recordings

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:27.380
into something creative while still staying grounded

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:28.660
in the original scenes.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:32.120
Now let's move to some cool stuff you can try right now

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:33.880
with tools that are already free.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:37.880
Some people online are sharing beautiful nostalgia style

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:40.460
AI videos that look like old home movies.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:43.980
The trick is feeding the AI good reference images

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:47.040
and then asking it to add motion that feels natural.

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:51.320
Go to Microsoft's Bing Image Creator or Google's Gemini

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:53.160
both of which have free versions.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:56.380
Upload a clear photo of yourself or a friend.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:00.860
Then type a prompt like turn this into a 1990s home video

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:03.300
with slight film grain and warm colors,

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.100
gentle movement like an old camcorder.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.260
Experiment with different decades or art styles

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:10.420
to see what works best.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:13.140
The results can be surprisingly fun

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:15.320
for school projects, birthday videos,

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.300
or just messing around with friends.

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:20.720
Next you can see how an AI checks its own facts

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:22.120
before making things up.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:25.520
A new tool called Keyron is designed to say

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:27.680
I do not know instead of guessing

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:29.300
when it cannot prove something.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:33.200
Visit the demo page at the site mentioned in the show notes

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:35.780
and type in a short claim like elephants

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:37.460
can jump higher than giraffes.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:40.020
Watch how the system labels each part

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.320
as verified refuted or refused.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:46.160
It is a cool way to see what careful checking looks like

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:48.480
before AI starts making up sources.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:51.560
In one quick bit, a user asked an AI

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.780
to prove that elephants can throw lions.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:57.260
The AI responded with a link to a fake video

00:04:57.260 --> 00:04:59.100
created using the Sora system.

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:02.580
Even after being informed that the video was generated

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:05.820
by AI, the original system defended the content.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:09.200
This example highlights how fabricated material

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.540
can quickly appear as credible evidence.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:14.560
The issue arises when no one verifies

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:17.260
the original source of the information provided.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:20.240
Such incidents point to growing concerns

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:23.880
about AI referencing other AI outputs without checks.

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:26.300
The story was shared on Reddit

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.140
in a discussion about concerning AI behaviors.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:32.880
In another quick bit, researchers have begun using AI

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.220
to solve longstanding math questions

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:36.500
that had remained open.

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:40.520
These breakthroughs come from applying similar AI techniques

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:42.600
to complex problems in mathematics.

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:45.980
Experts expect the same approach to extend

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:48.000
into fields like science and history.

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:51.180
Any area with difficult unsolved problems

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:53.560
could see rapid advances through these methods.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:55.920
For students, this development suggests

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:57.700
that homework tools may evolve

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:00.320
to address questions beyond standard textbooks.

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:02.940
The progress indicates a shift

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:06.280
where AI assists in pushing the boundaries of human knowledge.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:09.460
The update was posted on X by a researcher

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:11.400
tracking these AI capabilities.

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:12.820
And that's a wrap.

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:15.320
If any of today's stories made you go,

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.380
huh, that's cool, go play with it.

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:20.360
Curiosity is how every expert started.

